          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The program’s first gate is a finite-resolution comparison: can Jensen polynomials resolve a useful zero window at a reasonable cost compared with direct evaluation? I’ll start there. The existing results already show why finite surface topology alone cannot establish simplicity.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
