          "create_time": 1792605237.963,
          "update_time": 1792605240.589,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I’ve chosen a small window around the zero near height 14.1347, with a radius of \\(10^{-3}\\) in the program’s \\(s\\)-coordinate. I’ll compare complete error bounds and acquisition costs there. A large Jensen degree may still be cheap to evaluate locally if the unused coefficients have a certified tail bound, so I’ll test that before treating degree as a cost barrier.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
          "end_turn": false,
