          "update_time": 1792605433.336,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The first calculations show a large degree requirement from the inherited error bound, but only a small coefficient prefix appears necessary for local evaluation. They also exposed a precision cost: the central xi-series calculation loses accuracy through cancellation. I’m including extra working precision in the cost comparison and checking every resulting error bound with interval arithmetic.\n"
            ]
          },
