          "update_time": 1792605612.662,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Both methods now certify one simple zero in the chosen disk. The Jensen method works with 65 retained coefficients despite a degree above 200 billion, but its complete computation took about 39 times as long as direct evaluation in these runs.\n\nI’ll make one bounded refinement using the program’s sharper remainder formula to see how much of that degree requirement comes from the coarse error estimate.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
