          "update_time": 1792605935.493,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The sharper estimate reduces the sufficient degree from about 203 billion to 46 million—a factor of 4,414—while keeping the same \\(10^{-9}\\) approximation-error target. That is a useful improvement, though direct evaluation remains faster for this window.\n\nThe double-zero control also passes: its finite Jensen polynomials have separated simple roots while the limiting function retains a double zero. I’m saving the derivation, numerical record, and scope of the result, then updating the progress note.\n"
            ]
          },
          "status": "finished_successfully",
