          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Completed the first research round.\n\nA sharper bound reduces the sufficient Jensen degree from **203 billion to 46 million**, using **65 coefficients** with certified error bounds. Direct evaluation remained **17–39 times faster** in this pilot. The controls confirm that simple finite Jensen roots can coexist with a multiple limiting zero.\n\nSaved the [research note](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/13_contradiction_analysis/04_boundary_winding/threshold_routes/15_jensen_surface_degeneration/notes/01_LOCAL_RESOLUTION_AND_COMPLETE_COST_COMPARISON_20261021.md), numerical checks, and self-review; updated the [progress register](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/13_contradiction_analysis/04_boundary_winding/threshold_routes/15_jensen_surface_degeneration/research-progress/01_JENSEN_SURFACE_DEGENERATION_PROGRESS_20261021.md); and registered this chat in `chat-histories/`.\n\nThe broader program remains in reserve pending a distinct benefit beyond this single-window comparison. No global simplicity result is claimed."
            ]
          },
